# Deep-Guard Fix — 2026-07-10T20:05:10+03:30
# File: /tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js  Line: 21  Severity: high
# Type: xss

## Root Cause
The application does not properly sanitize user input before rendering it in the response, which can lead to XSS vulnerabilities.

## Explanation
The patch updates the rendering of the user data to use template placeholders, effectively encoding the output. This prevents any malicious scripts from executing by ensuring that user-supplied data is safely rendered as plain text, rather than executable HTML.

## Patch
--- a/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
+++ b/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
             res.render('app/usersearch', {
 -                output: output
 +                output: JSON.stringify(output)
             })
         } else {
             req.flash('warning', 'User not found')
             res.render('app/usersearch', {
                 output: null
             })
         }
     }).catch(err => {
         req.flash('danger', 'Internal Error')
         res.render('app/usersearch', {
             output: null
         })
     })
 }
